// FINDING 6 — a transparent `type` alias is not transparent for standard
// collections, in two separate ways.
//
// SPEC 4.4: "A module-level `type` alias is transparent."
// LEDGER 4.4 records test evidence as compile-pass only, so the run-pass path
// was never covered.
//
// Expected: compiles; prints 2.
// Actual (a): a method call on an alias-annotated binding checks cleanly but
//             fails lowering:
//               error: an expression whose type belongs to a later milestone
//               is not supported by the Milestone 8 executable subset
// Actual (b): merely routing a collection value through an alias annotation
//             makes the backend emit an unused constructor, which the
//             driver's own -Werror build rejects:
//               error: 'el_map_new_t60' defined but not used
//               [-Werror=unused-function]
//
// Both reproduce for `Vec` aliases as well. Assignment across the alias with
// no alias-annotated binding in between is fine.

type Registry[V] = Map[str, V]

fn main():
    var aliased: Registry[i32] = @map{"a": 1}
    aliased.insert("b", 2)
    println(f"{aliased.len()}")
